    x_petey_adjudication:
      verdict: proposed
      proposed: served_ind
      reason: The outlined box is a checkbox next to the caption 'I served the subpoena
        by delivering a copy to the named individual as follows:' — a filer checks
        or leaves it blank, making it a boolean indicator; 'served_ind' fits, 'service_status'
        (a category) does not.
      model: claude-sonnet-4-6
      contested: a witness says this widget's text belongs to another field
    x_petey_review:
      model: claude-opus-5
      changed:
      - type
      - description
      - -values
      - name
      reason: This is a single checkbox marking the 'I served the subpoena...' option,
        so a boolean indicator is correct; the category values 'served'/'Returned'
        describe two different checkboxes and the vague name does not say what ticking
        the box means.
      before:
        type: category
        values:
        - served
        - Returned
        description: Method of service
      old_name: service_status
      adjudicated: proposed
      judged: 'kept: 0 -> 0'
